message.content:
Looking at this task, I need to implement a hysteresis-based alarm handler in Structured Text (ST) for industrial automation.

Let me create the ST implementation:

```st
FUNCTION_BLOCK AlarmHandler
VAR_INPUT
    Value       : REAL;
    hiLevel     : REAL;
    loLevel     : REAL;
    hystWindow  : REAL;
END_VAR

VAR_OUTPUT
    hiAlarm     : BOOL;
    loAlarm     : BOOL;
    error       : BOOL;
    status      : WORD;
END_VAR

// Error checking
IF loLevel >= hiLevel THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8001;
    RETURN;
END_IF

IF hystWindow >= (hiLevel - loLevel) THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8002;
    RETURN;
END_IF

// No error
error := FALSE;
status := 16#0000;

// High alarm with hysteresis
// Trigger: Value > hiLevel
// Reset:   Value < hiLevel - hystWindow
IF Value > hiLevel THEN
    hiAlarm := TRUE;
ELSIF Value < (hiLevel - hystWindow) THEN
    hiAlarm := FALSE;
END_IF

// Low alarm with hysteresis
// Trigger: Value < loLevel
// Reset:   Value > loLevel + hystWindow
IF Value < loLevel THEN
    loAlarm := TRUE;
ELSIF Value > (loLevel + hystWindow) THEN
    loAlarm := FALSE;
END_IF

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```

This implementation:

- **Error handling:** Checks parameter validity before processing, returning specific error codes (16#8001 for invalid level range, 16#8002 for invalid hysteresis window)
- **High alarm:** Triggers when value exceeds hiLevel, resets when value drops below hiLevel - hystWindow
- **Low alarm:** Triggers when value drops below loLevel, resets when value rises above loLevel + hystWindow
- **Maintains state:** Uses the retained nature of output variables in function blocks to maintain alarm states between cycles

